<title>HUNGARY: Hungary Jan-June real wages up 5.4 pct y/y - CSO.</title>
<headline>Hungary Jan-June real wages up 5.4 pct y/y - CSO.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's net real wages rose an inflation-adjusted 5.4 percent in January-June from a year ago, the Central Statistical Office (CSO) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Net real wages for the first half were 37,530 forints ($187) per month while gross wages were 56,230 forints, up 22.4 percent year-on-year, the CSO said in a statement.</p>
<p>In the first half, wages in the telecommunications sector grew most, by 30.5 percent, it added.</p>
<p>Average June net wages were the highest in the financial sector with 66,627 forints, followed by the chemical sector with 49,602 forints, mining with 47,068 forints and utilities with 46,693 forints.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040 ($ = 200.5 Hungarian Forints)</p>
